{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/indexingiterator"]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"externalID":"s:s16IndexingIteratorV","platforms":[{"name":"iOS","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"8.0"},{"name":"iPadOS","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"8.0"},{"name":"Mac Catalyst","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"13.0"},{"name":"macOS","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"10.10"},{"name":"tvOS","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"9.0"},{"name":"visionOS","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"1.0"},{"name":"watchOS","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"2.0"}],"title":"IndexingIterator","roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","modules":[{"name":"Swift"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"IndexingIterator","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IndexingIterator","kind":"identifier"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that iterates over a collection using its indices."}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/IndexingIterator","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Type-Aliases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/IndexingIterator\/SubSequence"],"generated":true,"title":"Type Aliases"},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/IndexingIterator\/IteratorProtocol-Implementations","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/IndexingIterator\/Sequence-Implementations"],"generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Indices-and-Iterators","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/IteratorSequence","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/EnumeratedIterator","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/SetIterator","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/StrideThroughIterator","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/StrideToIterator"],"generated":true,"title":"Indices and Iterators"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IndexingIterator","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Elements"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Elements","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Collection","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl","text":"Collection","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"IndexingIterator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type is the default iterator for any collection that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"doesn’t declare its own. It acts as an iterator by using a collection’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indices to step over each value in the collection. Most collections in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"standard library use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IndexingIterator"},{"type":"text","text":" as their iterator."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"By default, any custom collection type you create will inherit a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"makeIterator()"},{"type":"text","text":" method that returns an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IndexingIterator"},{"type":"text","text":" instance,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"making it unnecessary to declare your own. When creating a custom"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collection type, add the minimal requirements of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Collection"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"protocol: starting and ending indices and a subscript for accessing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements. With those elements defined, the inherited "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"makeIterator()"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"method satisfies the requirements of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sequence"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Here’s an example of a type that declares the minimal requirements for a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collection. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectionOfTwo"},{"type":"text","text":" structure is a fixed-size collection"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that always holds two elements of a specific type."}]},{"code":["struct CollectionOfTwo<Element>: Collection {","    let elements: (Element, Element)","","    init(_ first: Element, _ second: Element) {","        self.elements = (first, second)","    }","","    var startIndex: Int { return 0 }","    var endIndex: Int   { return 2 }","","    subscript(index: Int) -> Element {","        switch index {","        case 0: return elements.0","        case 1: return elements.1","        default: fatalError(\"Index out of bounds.\")","        }","    }","    ","    func index(after i: Int) -> Int {","        precondition(i < endIndex, \"Can't advance beyond endIndex\")","        return i + 1","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectionOfTwo"},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t define its own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"makeIterator()"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"method or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Iterator"},{"type":"text","text":" associated type, it uses the default iterator type,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IndexingIterator"},{"type":"text","text":". This example shows how a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectionOfTwo"},{"type":"text","text":" instance"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be created holding the values of a point, and then iterated over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"using a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for"},{"type":"text","text":"-"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"in"},{"type":"text","text":" loop."}]},{"code":["let point = CollectionOfTwo(15.0, 20.0)","for element in point {","    print(element)","}","\/\/ Prints \"15.0\"","\/\/ Prints \"20.0\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Copyable","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Escapable","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/IteratorProtocol","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Sendable","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/SendableMetatype","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Sequence"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"references":{"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/IteratorProtocol":{"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IteratorProtocol","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A type that supplies the values of a sequence one at a time.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"IteratorProtocol","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"IteratorProtocol","kind":"symbol","conformance":{"constraints":[{"code":"Elements","type":"cod